d providerConfiguration data and AC4 specifies Keychain accessibility and access group, exactly what G4 and K2 decide. Gate R37 plus a new D1 block in check-portal-consumer.py reading blockedBy for tasks AND bugs make a missing edge fail closed; reachability is transitive; done is explicitly NOT an exemption basis because having finished is evidence a consumer RAN, which is the failure D1 catches; the one upstream exemption is verified upstream rather than accepted. RULE N1: the other half of the count class r6 left open - section 9.1 records it biting already, r3's prose claiming a number over a list holding a different one, r4 correcting it by hand, r5 moving it again when K2 withdrew the keychain group, while r6's scan covers App Group RECORD counts only. N1 derives allowlist counts and the rendered key list from the rows in both artifacts, pins its exclusion lists because widening an exclusion is the quiet way to neuter a scan, and states its bound rather than implying completeness. Three defects in the NEW gates were found by their own negative mutations and fixed rather than worked around: R37's reverse check was TAUTOLOGICAL because it counted the consumers list itself as a mention, so appending a consumer id present nowhere else passed; a graph mutation premised on cutting 3jloqy's edge orphaned nothing because q5kjta also blocks it and carries its own edge, so the premise was wrong rather than the gate, and it is also the argument for a closure over an edge check; and a document mutation did not apply against a hard-wrapped sentence. The fixed reverse check immediately found TASK-260715-33oofa - a declared consumer the contract never explained, its obligation stated inside the macOS task's entry while 33oofa is the iOS half carrying the opposite instruction - now recorded. Also recorded, not smoothed over: the board resource store does not preserve the executable bit, so a re-registered .sh exits 126 on a ./ run and must be invoked via zsh. Gates: validate_matrix.py 37 rules 2483 checks exit 0; mutate.py 202/202 negative gates exit 0 (38 new - 20 D1, 18 N1 - including a new dependency-GRAPH harness, because D1's reachability half cannot be tested by corrupting the contract, which is why eight revisions of a 1331-check validator never saw it); check-portal-consumer.py 84 checks over 3 rules exit 0; preserve.py 122 assertions exit 0, including a top-level check that the only keys ADDED are consumerDependencyContract and numericClaimContract and the only keys CHANGED are revision, supersedes, revisionLog, consumers and downstreamConsequences; an independent gate that imports no project harness flips r8 false/exit 1 to r9 true/exit 0; check-legacy-preservation.sh exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; swift test 335 tests in 29 suites exit 0. All four matrix harnesses re-verified running in place from the board resource layout; every command run without a pipeline because zsh carries no PIPESTATUS. No entitlement decision, target row, profile row, record, assertion, assertion scope or C1 mutation set changed. Board footprint: one dependency edge added, and one field on one element - TASK-260728-q5kjta.scope, revision label r8 to r9, character delta 0, verified byte-exact, required by amendmentRule. No board element created, deleted, re-parented or re-scoped; no portal mutation; no product source, spec file or generated project touched. Ready for review.
